Before implementation, I want to make a few improvements so that the Course Service remains scalable, reusable, and maintainable across the entire microservices ecosystem.

===========================================================
GENERAL REQUIREMENTS
===========================================================

Analyze the complete course-service before making any changes.

Do NOT regenerate the project.

Do NOT rewrite unrelated code.

Modify ONLY

common-library

course-service

Update user-service imports only if required because security classes are moved to common-library.

Do NOT modify

auth-service

api-gateway

content-service

enrollment-service

frontend-service

===========================================================
COMMON LIBRARY
===========================================================

Move only reusable security infrastructure into common-library.

This should include

UserPrincipal

HeaderAuthenticationFilter

AuthenticatedUserProvider

SecurityConstants

JwtHeaderNames

Any reusable authentication utility classes

Do NOT place any business logic inside common-library.

The common-library must remain framework-independent as much as possible.

===========================================================
COURSE OWNERSHIP
===========================================================

Every Course must have

ownerId

This value must always come from the authenticated UserPrincipal.

Never accept

ownerId

instructorId

creatorId

createdBy

or any ownership field from the client.

The frontend must never specify course ownership.

===========================================================
AUTHORIZATION
===========================================================

Use Spring Security method-level authorization.

Enable

@EnableMethodSecurity

Use

@PreAuthorize

where appropriate.

Avoid manual role comparisons whenever possible.

